## Finding description and impact

The setTokenizeFee() function in the UpsideProtocol contract allows the contract owner to set arbitrarily large tokenize fees for any supported token without enforcing a maximum limit. This unchecked value is later directly used in safeTransferFrom() during the tokenize() call, which can lead to significant or total user fund loss.

 /// @notice Allows Owner to set tokenize fee per token address
    /// @param _tokenizeFeeAddress Token address to set
    /// @param _tokenizeFeeAmount Tokenize fee amount for this tokenize fee address
    function setTokenizeFee(address _tokenizeFeeAddress, uint256 _tokenizeFeeAmount) external onlyOwner {
        tokenizeFeeMap[_tokenizeFeeAddress] = _tokenizeFeeAmount;
        emit TokenizeFeeSet(_tokenizeFeeAddress, _tokenizeFeeAmount);
    }


Problem:
Since the lower bound is checked on the Fee Amount in the tokenization(), there is no upper limit check in setTokenizeFee(). A malicious or negligent owner could set the fee to a very large value (e.g. type(uint256).max), causing users to unknowingly attempt to transfer excessive or total balances when calling tokenize().This could come to light in scenario where the owner is compromised since the function is protected.


 Impact

    Severity:  Medium

    Impact type: User fund loss / protocol usability risk . This may cause DoS attack for the protocol users if this set happens and eventually fund loss for the protocol in the long-run


    Risk examples:

        Owner sets fee to 1e77 for USDC.

        User tries to tokenize a URL with a valid tokenizeFeeEnabled token.

        safeTransferFrom() drains all approved USDC from the user's wallet



## Recommended mitigation steps
Implement a maximum cap when setting fees, or require an admin review flow:

uint256 public constant MAX_TOKENIZE_FEE = 1_000_000e18; // Or another reasonable upper bound

function setTokenizeFee(address _tokenizeFeeAddress, uint256 _tokenizeFeeAmount) external onlyOwner {
    if (_tokenizeFeeAmount > MAX_TOKENIZE_FEE) {
        revert TokenizeFeeTooHigh();
    }
    tokenizeFeeMap[_tokenizeFeeAddress] = _tokenizeFeeAmount;
    emit TokenizeFeeSet(_tokenizeFeeAddress, _tokenizeFeeAmount);
}

