## Summary

The function `getCirculatingSupplyAndAssets` is used during share-to-asset and asset-to-share conversions. It relies on `totalInvestmentAssets`, which includes `rBalance` from the investment share token. However, `rBalance` is not stable and can be reversed via `WERC7575ShareToken::cancelrBalanceAdjustment`. If `rBalance` is later corrected, users whose deposits or redemptions were executed based on the incorrect value will receive inaccurate share amounts or asset amounts, effectively causing value shifts between users.

## Root Cause

`_calculateInvestmentAssets` adds both the investment share token balance and its `rBalance`:

```solidity
// Add invested assets from the investment ShareToken (if configured)
totalNormalizedAssets += _calculateInvestmentAssets();

// _calculateInvestmentAssets
function _calculateInvestmentAssets() internal view returns (uint256 totalInvestmentAssets) {
    ShareTokenStorage storage $ = _getShareTokenStorage();
    address investmentShareToken = $.investmentShareToken;

    if (investmentShareToken == address(0)) {
        return 0;
    }

    // Balance of investment ShareToken (normalized to 18 decimals)
    totalInvestmentAssets = IERC20(investmentShareToken).balanceOf(address(this));

    // Add rBalance if supported
    try IWERC7575ShareToken(investmentShareToken).rBalanceOf(address(this)) returns (uint256 rShares) {
        totalInvestmentAssets += rShares;
    } catch {
        // Ignore if rBalanceOf is not supported
    }
}
```

However, `rBalance` is not immutable. It can be reverted through `cancelrBalanceAdjustment`:

```solidity
function cancelrBalanceAdjustment(address account, uint256 ts) external onlyRevenueAdmin {
    if (_rBalanceAdjustments[account][ts][0] == 0) {
        revert NoRBalanceAdjustmentFound();
    }

    uint256[2] memory adjustment = _rBalanceAdjustments[account][ts];
    uint256 amounti = adjustment[0];
    uint256 amountr = adjustment[1];

    if (amountr > amounti) {
        uint256 difference = amountr - amounti;
        uint256 currentRBalance = _rBalances[account];
        if (currentRBalance < difference) {
            revert RBalanceAdjustmentTooLarge();
        } else {
            unchecked {
                _rBalances[account] -= difference;
            }
        }
    } else if (amountr < amounti) {
        uint256 difference = amounti - amountr;
        unchecked {
            _rBalances[account] += difference;
        }
    }

    delete _rBalanceAdjustments[account][ts];
    emit RBalanceAdjustmentCancelled(account, ts);
}
```

Because deposits and redemptions use this value at execution time, any later correction to `rBalance` introduces inconsistency and unintended wealth transfer between users.

## Mitigation

Do not include `rBalance` in investment asset calculations, as these balances are not realized. Only add them once they are fully realized and reflected in the actual vault asset balance. This prevents reversible or incorrect `rBalance` adjustments from corrupting share conversion logic.

---

